WEBVTT

00:05.388 --> 00:08.983
I really appreciate you getting up so early
and driving me to work.

00:12.128 --> 00:13.618
I owe you one. Heh.

00:14.164 --> 00:18.066
You owed me one
when I didn't smother you in your crib.

00:19.669 --> 00:21.864
Well, then I owe you two. Ha, ha.

00:22.772 --> 00:25.366
My car will be out of the shop
in a couple of days. There was a-

00:25.542 --> 00:27.703
A terrible knock in the engine. Like a:

00:30.213 --> 00:32.909
I kept saying, "Come in," but nobody did.
Ha-ha-ha.

00:33.917 --> 00:35.509
Ooh, carpool lane. That's us. We should-

00:35.685 --> 00:37.152
- Shut up.
- Right.

00:39.622 --> 00:42.386
It's 7:00.
Where are all these damn people going?

00:42.559 --> 00:46.051
Ha, I know, right?
I deal with that every day.

00:46.229 --> 00:47.628
It's very frustrating.

00:47.797 --> 00:50.595
Sometimes I dream
about buying a cabin in the woods and-

00:50.767 --> 00:52.860
- I said shut up.
- Yes, you did.

00:55.638 --> 00:59.074
People going that way should switch jobs
with the people going this way...

00:59.242 --> 01:01.642
...and everybody can leave
their freaking cars in the garage.

01:02.979 --> 01:05.243
You know, that's a-
That's a hell of an idea.

01:05.415 --> 01:06.575
Right on. Ha, ha.

01:07.417 --> 01:09.214
- Don't patronize me.
- Sorry.

01:13.256 --> 01:16.350
Wait a minute.
How are you getting back to Malibu?

01:17.727 --> 01:19.922
- Uh, I was- Uh, I was hoping- Charlie.
- No.

01:20.096 --> 01:22.690
- Take the bus.
- There's no bus from Tarzana to Malibu.

01:22.866 --> 01:25.300
Then take a series of busses.

01:25.535 --> 01:27.469
And don't get stuck
on having to end up in Malibu.

01:27.637 --> 01:28.934
Ugh, Charlie-

01:29.105 --> 01:31.335
Come on. It's just for a couple of days.

01:31.508 --> 01:34.033
That's what Mom said when she brought
you home from the hospital.

01:35.979 --> 01:37.469
Good one.

01:38.448 --> 01:40.177
You're a very funny man, Ollie.

01:41.084 --> 01:42.244
You certainly are.

01:45.155 --> 01:46.884
It's- Laurel and Hardy.

01:47.323 --> 01:49.883
Boy, they used to-
They used to get in some wacky jams, huh?

01:52.061 --> 01:54.188
Oh, what about, uh, Abbott and Costello?

01:55.064 --> 01:56.395
Hey, Abbott!

01:58.334 --> 02:00.063
Or, uh- Or, uh, Martin and Lewis.
You know-

02:00.236 --> 02:01.533
Hey, lady!

02:01.704 --> 02:05.140
With the flavin and the maving
and the wow.

02:08.077 --> 02:10.272
Three Stooges? Nyuck, nyuck, nyuck.

02:13.783 --> 02:15.114
Whoa, why are we stopping?

02:15.285 --> 02:16.650
Ow, ow, ow!

02:16.820 --> 02:19.050
Oh, a wise guy. Ow!

02:22.358 --> 02:25.088
Okay, I don't mind the good-natured
brotherly punching...

02:25.261 --> 02:27.593
...but you did not have
to twist my nipples.

02:28.331 --> 02:31.630
You're lucky I didn't rip them off
and feed them to you.

02:31.801 --> 02:35.567
Um, if you have to go to the bathroom,
there's one down the hallway.

02:35.905 --> 02:38.635
- What's wrong with the one in your office?
- Uh, it's not for guests.

02:38.808 --> 02:40.105
Neither is my house.

02:40.577 --> 02:42.909
Um, I think we're out of paper towels.

02:43.079 --> 02:45.240
I'll wipe my hands on you.
Get out of the way.

02:48.651 --> 02:50.516
Morning, Dr. Harper.

02:50.687 --> 02:52.279
Morning, Melissa.

02:53.456 --> 02:55.424
Hello, Melissa.

02:58.228 --> 03:00.093
You rat bastard.

03:28.725 --> 03:30.989
The bathroom is down the hallway
on the right.

03:31.160 --> 03:32.821
Good to know.

03:33.229 --> 03:35.493
Hi. I'm Charlie, Alan's brother.

03:35.665 --> 03:37.599
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you too.

03:37.767 --> 03:40.099
- Thought you had to tinkle.
- Go away.

03:41.671 --> 03:44.162
So how long have you been working
for my baby brother?

03:44.807 --> 03:46.240
About six months.

03:46.409 --> 03:50.072
Wow. He's been keeping you a secret
for six months?

03:52.081 --> 03:54.015
Charlie, can I talk to you for a minute?

03:54.183 --> 03:56.913
There's no reason to thank me
for the ride again, Alan.

03:57.086 --> 03:59.384
&lt;i>Mi Mercedes, su Mercedes.&lt;/i>

04:01.524 --> 04:05.585
It's what brothers do when one
is vastly more fortunate than the other.

04:07.430 --> 04:08.954
Seriously, we need to talk.

04:10.934 --> 04:12.060
Excuse us.

04:15.104 --> 04:19.632
- She is the best receptionist I've ever had.
- I'm hoping to say the same.

04:19.809 --> 04:22.243
God, Charlie, please do not crap
where I work.

04:22.412 --> 04:23.970
Hey, you crap where I live.

04:25.214 --> 04:27.614
- So tell me about her.
- Oh, there's nothing to tell.

04:27.784 --> 04:30.776
She's, uh- She's a terrific employee.
She does my scheduling, my books.

04:30.954 --> 04:34.219
My patients love her. She keeps
the operation running like clockwork...

04:34.390 --> 04:37.621
...and she does it all
for crappy pay and no benefits.

04:39.429 --> 04:40.828
So you're not hitting that?

04:41.331 --> 04:42.491
No, I'm not hitting that.

04:42.665 --> 04:46.101
And even if I were hitting that,
I wouldn't use the phrase "hitting that."

04:46.269 --> 04:48.237
It's a violent image for a beautiful act.

04:48.404 --> 04:50.269
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So the coast is clear?

04:50.440 --> 04:51.702
No, the coast is not clear.

04:51.874 --> 04:55.002
The coast is foggy and strewn
with dangerously pointy rocks.

04:56.346 --> 04:58.337
Can I get either of you a cup of coffee?

04:58.514 --> 04:59.572
- No.
- Sure.

05:00.917 --> 05:03.351
No for both of us. Please leave.

05:03.519 --> 05:05.009
All right.

05:05.188 --> 05:06.951
- Bye, Melissa.
- Bye, Charlie.

05:07.123 --> 05:08.420
Hope I see you again.

05:08.825 --> 05:12.022
Oh, you'll see me tonight
when I come back to pick up your boss.

05:12.996 --> 05:16.454
Oh. Oh, no, Charlie. You don't have to make
that long drive. I'll take the bus.

05:16.632 --> 05:20.466
- I thought there were no busses.
- If I have to, I'll charter one.

05:21.104 --> 05:22.867
Why don't I just give you a ride home?

05:23.773 --> 05:26.333
Oh, that is so sweet of you.

05:26.509 --> 05:29.069
You got a real gem here, Alan.

05:29.245 --> 05:31.509
Tell you what,
when you get him home...

05:31.681 --> 05:34.878
...there'll be a cold margarita
waiting for you out on my deck.

05:35.785 --> 05:37.582
Which overlooks the ocean.

05:37.754 --> 05:39.312
On the beach.

05:39.489 --> 05:41.320
In Malibu.

05:42.392 --> 05:43.620
That sounds wonderful.

05:43.793 --> 05:46.785
It's really not. It's chilly, damp
and covered with pelican poop.

05:48.498 --> 05:51.194
That's why he'll never win
the Malibu-slogan contest.

05:51.367 --> 05:53.028
Ha, ha! Ahem.

05:53.536 --> 05:55.868
- See you tonight, Melissa.
- Bye, Charlie.

05:56.039 --> 05:57.836
- Have a great day, bro.
- I hate you.

05:58.007 --> 05:59.235
I hate you too.

06:01.511 --> 06:03.376
Gee, your brother is really cute.

06:03.546 --> 06:05.480
As a bug.

06:07.216 --> 06:09.980
- Bathroom?
- Oh, let me give you the key.

06:14.657 --> 06:18.024
- Thank you.
- You're very welcome.

06:18.661 --> 06:20.891
You are a doll.

06:21.230 --> 06:23.095
You are cute.

06:28.704 --> 06:30.899
She's actually a doll.

06:33.810 --> 06:36.904
I wonder if she's anatomically correct.

06:47.890 --> 06:49.915
Who's the Smurf?

06:52.328 --> 06:54.592
The Smurf is my receptionist.

06:55.164 --> 06:56.688
You're letting Charlie hit that?

06:58.401 --> 07:00.699
Okay, first of all,
that is a very ugly phrase.

07:00.870 --> 07:02.462
And second, I'm not letting him.

07:02.638 --> 07:05.835
Short of drugging him and dumping
him in the woods, what can I do?

07:06.008 --> 07:09.171
Yeah. He is like an Alabama bloodhound
once he gets a whiff.

07:13.149 --> 07:16.607
Now it's just a matter of waiting
till it blows up in my face.

07:16.786 --> 07:21.382
And after it blows up in my face, it will
then circle around and bite me in the ass.

07:21.891 --> 07:25.292
That's me. No face, no ass.

07:25.561 --> 07:28.291
Well, that's what you get
when you mix work and personal.

07:28.731 --> 07:32.428
Which is why me and Charlie have always
kept everything strictly professional.

07:35.304 --> 07:37.829
Yeah.
Yeah, I've often wondered about that.

07:38.007 --> 07:42.501
When I first started work here,
I laid down the law: Lookie, no touchy.

07:47.984 --> 07:49.008
Yipes.

07:51.354 --> 07:55.347
All right. I'll make you another,
but you gotta promise not to chug this one.

07:55.525 --> 07:57.459
Promise.

07:59.295 --> 08:01.354
What a fun gal.

08:01.697 --> 08:04.598
Do you know how hard it is
to find a decent receptionist?

08:04.767 --> 08:07.133
Well, kudos, bro. You did a great job.

08:08.337 --> 08:10.601
Thank you.
And I really don't wanna lose her.

08:10.907 --> 08:13.273
- Why would you lose her?
- Oh, gee, I don't know.

08:13.442 --> 08:17.208
Maybe because my brother intends to defile
and discard her like a warm melon.

08:18.147 --> 08:19.444
A warm melon?

08:20.616 --> 08:22.049
Nothing.

08:22.351 --> 08:23.682
Anyway, my point is...

08:23.853 --> 08:27.016
...uh, you're gonna leave her with memories
that can only be erased...

08:27.190 --> 08:30.717
...by removing herself from anything
that reminds her of you. Like me.

08:31.027 --> 08:35.020
- Is that what you're worried about, Bunky?
- Yes, that's what I'm worried about.

08:35.198 --> 08:38.031
What did you think?
What else would I be worried about?

08:38.668 --> 08:39.862
Well, let's see.

08:40.036 --> 08:42.368
Your receding hairline,
your semiliterate son...

08:42.538 --> 08:46.235
...your budding man boobs,
but that's just off the top of my head.

08:46.642 --> 08:50.203
- Charlie, please, I- I am begging you-
- Look, I understand your concerns.

08:50.379 --> 08:52.574
It's not like that.
I think Melissa is terrific.

08:52.748 --> 08:56.616
Oh, you always think they're terrific.
They're terrific before, they're terrific during.

08:56.786 --> 08:58.981
It's the after when the crying
and quitting start.

08:59.155 --> 09:00.952
Why is it always about you?

09:01.123 --> 09:02.920
Aren't I entitled to some happiness?

09:04.460 --> 09:06.360
You've had your share of happiness.

09:06.529 --> 09:09.726
You've had your share of happiness,
my share, everybody's share.

09:10.533 --> 09:15.334
You've sucked the marrow of happiness
from the bones of-

09:15.504 --> 09:17.335
Oh, just leave her alone, won't you?

09:19.508 --> 09:23.342
Alan, you don't have to worry.
You're thinking about the old Charlie.

09:23.512 --> 09:26.447
The old hump them and dump them,
one-track-mind Charlie.

09:26.616 --> 09:30.746
Oh. Oh, right. The old Charlie
from way back this morning.

09:30.920 --> 09:34.014
I'm serious. I honestly wanna start
building a relationship.

09:34.190 --> 09:36.215
- Really?
- Yeah. Get to know someone.

09:36.392 --> 09:39.759
Let her get to know me, have something
in common before we jump into bed.

09:39.929 --> 09:42.727
- Wow. I'm impressed.
- That I'm growing up?

09:42.898 --> 09:45.389
No, that you can so easily lie to my face.

09:46.902 --> 09:49.996
You'll see.
It's gonna be different with Melissa.

09:50.172 --> 09:52.766
I'm gonna take my time,
form a friendship...

09:52.942 --> 09:57.038
...bond emotionally and then, and only then,
take it to the next level.

09:59.548 --> 10:02.244
MELISSA:
Oh, Charlie.

10:05.821 --> 10:08.585
You schmuck.

10:16.464 --> 10:18.591
Morning, Dr. Harper.

10:21.002 --> 10:22.469
Morning.

10:22.671 --> 10:25.640
I like your jammies.

10:25.807 --> 10:28.105
Thank you. I, uh- I like your-

10:28.276 --> 10:29.834
Thank you.

10:31.546 --> 10:33.514
Guess you're kind of surprised
to see me, huh?

10:33.682 --> 10:35.673
Yeah, shocked.

10:35.850 --> 10:39.946
Well, I hope you know
it is not the kind of thing I usually do.

10:40.121 --> 10:43.522
You know, hop into bed
with a fella zippity quick.

10:43.858 --> 10:47.225
- It's really none of my business.
- Well, I don't.

10:47.395 --> 10:50.057
But Charlie is so sweet and special.

10:50.432 --> 10:52.832
Yep, he's a treasure.

10:54.603 --> 10:56.764
Yeah, and this works out well for you.

10:57.072 --> 10:58.562
Really? Uh, how do you figure?

10:58.940 --> 11:03.673
Since your car's still in the shop,
we can carpool to and from work.

11:04.212 --> 11:06.680
I see. So you'll be coming back?

11:06.848 --> 11:08.247
Oh, yeah.

11:08.416 --> 11:11.044
Charlie asked me to stay the weekend.

11:11.886 --> 11:13.751
- No kidding.
- Yeppers.

11:13.922 --> 11:16.254
We really made a connection.

11:16.424 --> 11:18.654
And it is not just physical.

11:18.827 --> 11:21.694
Although the physical part is amazing.

11:23.131 --> 11:25.361
Again, none of my business.

11:25.533 --> 11:27.626
It is like I have known him all my life.

11:28.036 --> 11:30.470
I know the feeling. You get over it.

11:31.673 --> 11:32.731
Hey, baby.

11:33.074 --> 11:34.735
Hey, yourself.

11:37.279 --> 11:39.042
Mm. Do I smell toast?

11:39.214 --> 11:43.310
You do. Would you like a slice?
I can put butter and jelly on it.

11:43.485 --> 11:45.146
Oh, déjà vu.

11:45.320 --> 11:46.844
MELISSA:
Ah! Stop it! Terrible.

11:47.022 --> 11:48.046
Whoo!

11:51.326 --> 11:53.624
Sorry, Dr. Harper.

11:53.928 --> 11:56.624
That's okay. I wasn't even listening.

11:58.166 --> 12:01.897
I'm gonna take a shower.
Hit the road in about 20 minutes?

12:02.070 --> 12:04.561
- I thought you were gonna call in sick.
- Shush!

12:04.739 --> 12:05.967
He's kidding. It's-

12:06.408 --> 12:08.273
It's okay. Twenty minutes is fine.

12:08.443 --> 12:09.910
Great.

12:12.747 --> 12:15.477
Alan, you know me as a cynical man...

12:15.650 --> 12:22.146
...but in just one night, that little pixie
has melted this cold, lonely heart.

12:32.667 --> 12:33.998
You don't say.

12:35.003 --> 12:37.801
You may not believe me,
but there is something going on here.

12:37.972 --> 12:40.497
I really wanna thank you
for bringing her into my life.

12:40.942 --> 12:42.967
I may not believe you.

12:43.445 --> 12:46.073
You know what? Fine.
Think what you want.

12:46.247 --> 12:47.976
Now, if you'll excuse me...

12:48.149 --> 12:51.118
...I'm gonna go play Paul Bunyan
Takes a Shower in Tiny Town.

12:57.158 --> 12:59.023
Sorry we're running late.

12:59.194 --> 13:00.923
That's all right.

13:01.096 --> 13:04.327
Shower lasted
a bit longer than I planned.

13:06.968 --> 13:09.459
Yeah, well, uh, that happens.

13:10.572 --> 13:13.803
I gotta tell you,
I am just crazy about your brother.

13:14.442 --> 13:15.466
Swell.

13:15.643 --> 13:17.634
Hope it works out.

13:18.680 --> 13:21.706
And how is a guy like that still single?

13:23.718 --> 13:27.552
Well, uh, he's always been a bit
of a butterfly, you know.

13:27.722 --> 13:31.089
Fluttering through life, hard to pin down.

13:31.493 --> 13:34.587
And being a fall-down drunk is kind of
a speed bump for some of the ladies.

13:35.930 --> 13:37.397
Such a jokester, Dr. Harper.

13:38.800 --> 13:42.031
Either that or put a gun in my mouth.

13:42.570 --> 13:45.266
Oh, listen. On the way home,
we have to swing by my apartment...

13:45.440 --> 13:47.169
...so I can get some clothes
for the weekend.

13:47.342 --> 13:48.331
Mm-hm.

13:48.510 --> 13:50.637
And I'm gonna need a little extra time
for lunch today.

13:50.812 --> 13:53.337
Wanna buy some sexy lingerie, heh...

13:53.515 --> 13:55.312
...for, you know.

13:56.484 --> 13:58.281
I do.

13:58.453 --> 14:00.353
Can I pick you up anything?

14:00.522 --> 14:04.424
Yeah, yeah, um, ear plugs would be nice.

14:04.592 --> 14:06.822
And that gun I mentioned.

14:07.762 --> 14:09.229
Nothing special.

14:09.397 --> 14:11.661
I'm only gonna use it just the once.

14:20.341 --> 14:23.435
- Hey, Jake.
- Hey. Gotta hit the crapper.

14:25.380 --> 14:26.745
You must be Judith.

14:26.915 --> 14:28.382
I'm sorry, do I know you?

14:28.550 --> 14:32.577
I'm Melissa, Dr. Harper's receptionist.
We talk on the phone all the time.

14:32.754 --> 14:35.154
Oh, right, Melissa.
It's nice to finally meet you.

14:35.323 --> 14:37.257
Alan!

14:37.425 --> 14:39.620
Oh. Oh, hey. Hey. Hi, uh, hi, Judith.

14:39.794 --> 14:41.523
This is Melissa. Melissa, Judith.

14:41.696 --> 14:44.324
It's not what it looks like.
Charlie's doing her, not me.

14:45.633 --> 14:48.830
- And, uh, where is Charlie anyway?
- Taking a nap.

14:49.003 --> 14:50.630
Hmm.
- He says I drain him.

14:52.273 --> 14:54.002
Isn't that adorable?

14:55.543 --> 14:58.205
Adorable, disturbing, whatever.

14:58.379 --> 14:59.937
Uh, thanks, I've got this.

15:01.483 --> 15:03.110
Your brother and your receptionist?

15:03.284 --> 15:05.809
What? The Volvo's in the shop.
He twisted my nipples...

15:05.987 --> 15:08.080
- ...and peed in my office.
- What?

15:08.256 --> 15:10.087
I'm not thrilled, but what can I do?

15:10.258 --> 15:13.455
You could think about the effect
these shenanigans have on your son.

15:13.761 --> 15:16.161
Okay, you know what, Judith?
I have enough problems.

15:16.331 --> 15:20.131
If you're not comfortable leaving Jake here
for the weekend, then take him home.

15:20.401 --> 15:21.959
Nice try, Alan.

15:29.677 --> 15:32.840
You think Uncle Charlie and Melissa
are coming down for lunch?

15:33.014 --> 15:34.606
I doubt it.

15:36.317 --> 15:38.649
- Can I have their chicken?
- Knock yourself out.

15:44.125 --> 15:46.116
You know how you say
I can ask you anything?

15:46.761 --> 15:49.059
- Yeah?
- Is them being together weird for you?

15:49.230 --> 15:50.356
No, no.

15:50.532 --> 15:52.159
Well, you're a better man than I.

15:56.504 --> 15:58.699
- How so?
- Well, remember when Uncle Charlie...

15:58.873 --> 16:01.205
- ...was hitting my fifth-grade teacher?
- Okay.

16:01.809 --> 16:04.243
Can we please stop calling it "hitting"?

16:04.412 --> 16:07.575
I got another word,
but I don't think you're gonna like it.

16:11.519 --> 16:17.082
Fine. Fine, then I do remember when
he was hitting your fifth-grade teacher.

16:17.458 --> 16:20.256
- That kind of bugged me.
- Well, I'm sorry.

16:20.595 --> 16:23.393
- Don't think there should be boundaries?
- I do think that.

16:24.098 --> 16:26.999
But I thought you said it's not weird
he's hitting your receptionist.

16:27.168 --> 16:31.195
Ah, uh, well, pal, um, the thing is, um...

16:31.606 --> 16:33.164
...Daddy lied.

16:33.908 --> 16:36.672
- Oh, then it is weird for you?
- Yes, yes, it's weird for me.

16:36.945 --> 16:38.879
- Are you jealous?
- Uh, no, no.

16:39.047 --> 16:42.574
Because I was a little bit jealous
about Miss Pasternak.

16:42.750 --> 16:44.047
She had a rocking bod.

16:46.087 --> 16:47.748
Eat your chicken.

16:53.061 --> 16:54.289
Melissa?

16:54.462 --> 16:58.193
We, uh, need to get a move on.
A lot of traffic, what with the rain and all.

16:58.366 --> 17:01.893
CHARLIE: We need a minute, Alan.
- Oh, God.

17:02.270 --> 17:05.569
What can they do in a minute
that they didn't do all weekend?

17:06.107 --> 17:08.405
MELISSA:
You are just a selfish son of a bitch...

17:08.576 --> 17:10.737
...and you can go right to hell!

17:12.614 --> 17:16.050
Sorry, Dr. Harper. I'll be in the car.

17:20.888 --> 17:23.288
Well, that could've gone better.

17:23.625 --> 17:24.717
I knew it.

17:24.892 --> 17:27.656
I thought it might take longer
than 48 hours, but I knew it.

17:27.829 --> 17:30.491
Hey, hey, hey.
A little sensitivity would be appreciated.

17:30.665 --> 17:31.893
I'm hurting here.

17:32.200 --> 17:34.327
I'm sure a lot of that is friction burn.

17:36.037 --> 17:40.064
- Whoa, whoa, where does that come from?
- Oh, where does it come from?

17:40.408 --> 17:44.811
It comes from a long history
of you using my life as a specimen cup.

17:45.313 --> 17:48.441
Excuse me,
but you're still talking about the old Charlie.

17:48.916 --> 17:52.249
This Charlie was hoping to have
a relationship of substance and depth.

17:52.420 --> 17:57.255
By locking a stranger in your room
and hitting it for two days straight?

17:58.459 --> 18:00.984
Okay, mea culpa.

18:02.230 --> 18:03.492
Change is hard.

18:04.999 --> 18:07.490
And now that I'm hearing it,
I agree with you.

18:07.669 --> 18:10.035
"Hitting it" is an ugly term.

18:10.438 --> 18:12.872
- Don't change the subject. What happened?
CHARLIE: Nothing.

18:16.277 --> 18:18.837
I just said to her
maybe we should slow things down...

18:19.013 --> 18:20.071
...see other people.

18:20.248 --> 18:22.614
What-? You said this after the two days?

18:23.117 --> 18:26.018
How could I know beforehand?

18:26.187 --> 18:30.123
I thought you'd be happy. You didn't want
me to go out with her in the first place.

18:30.291 --> 18:33.158
Yes, but it's no longer the first place.
It's the last place.

18:33.928 --> 18:36.692
What can I tell you, Alan?
I made a mistake.

18:36.864 --> 18:37.956
I rushed to love.

18:39.467 --> 18:40.695
No, no.

18:40.868 --> 18:43.462
Your mistake was you rushed to love
my receptionist.

18:43.638 --> 18:45.697
The woman I depend upon
to run my business.

18:45.873 --> 18:49.138
Oh, she's a good kid. She'll get over it.

18:50.912 --> 18:54.177
You hear that? Does that sound
like a woman who's getting over it?

18:54.348 --> 18:56.942
Well, Alan, the wounds are fresh.

18:57.118 --> 19:00.383
- You're gonna need to be patient.
- Why should I have to be patient?

19:00.555 --> 19:02.716
Well, you have to work with her.

19:05.493 --> 19:07.961
And it sounds like you better get going.

19:08.129 --> 19:11.929
Sure you don't wanna come back
to my office and hump my fax machine?

19:12.567 --> 19:15.400
Wow. You still have a fax machine?

19:16.204 --> 19:17.569
You're despicable.

19:18.573 --> 19:20.200
- Alan, wait.
- What?

19:20.608 --> 19:23.441
- Let me make it up to you.
- How could you make it up to me?

19:23.978 --> 19:28.278
Well, I'm guessing she won't be inclined
to bring you back here tonight...

19:28.449 --> 19:31.384
...so why don't you take a cab
and I'll pay for it?

19:31.786 --> 19:32.810
Thanks.

19:32.987 --> 19:34.852
That makes up for everything.

19:35.890 --> 19:38.859
I'm talking cab, not town car.

19:40.828 --> 19:42.125
Oh, man.

19:43.464 --> 19:46.331
Breakups are so hard.

19:48.436 --> 19:49.733
Ow!

19:50.304 --> 19:51.328
Huh.

19:52.006 --> 19:54.804
I do have a little friction burn.

20:03.017 --> 20:04.882
That miserable son of a bitch.

20:05.052 --> 20:08.453
You might wanna extend your brake zone
on the wet roads. It's a little-

20:08.623 --> 20:10.921
- I'm so stupid.
- No, no, no. You're not stupid.

20:11.092 --> 20:12.992
You're a dear, sweet, remarkably bright-

20:13.161 --> 20:15.322
Truck. Watch out for the truck!
Watch out for the truck!

20:22.436 --> 20:24.370
- I want a raise.
- Sure, sure.

20:24.539 --> 20:27.599
- And health insurance.
- A given. Can't believe you don't have it.

20:27.775 --> 20:29.902
- And a paid vacation.
- Hang on a second. There's only-

20:30.077 --> 20:32.375
Aah! Two weeks, two weeks, two weeks!
